answer:
To ensure that `fetchData` is called only when the user finishes typing in the `binding.tvSearch`, you can use a combination of `onFocusChangeListener` and `onKeyListener`. This approach will allow you to detect when the user starts typing and then call `fetchData` once they have finished typing.

Here's how you can modify your code:

```kotlin
binding.tvSearch.setOnFocusChangeListener { _, hasFocus ->
    if (!hasFocus) {
        // User has not focused on the input field yet
        return@setOnFocusChangeListener false

        // Start fetching data when focus changes
        binding.tvSearch.postDelayed({
            fetchData(binding.tvSearch.text.toString())
        }, DELAY)
    } else {
        // Focus changed, no need to start fetching data immediately
        return@setOnFocusChangeListener true
    }
}

// Define the delay time for fetching data
val DELAY = 1000L // 1 second
```

In this code:
- The `focusChangeListener` method checks whether the input field (`binding.tvSearch`) has been focused.
- If the input field hasn't been focused yet, it returns `false`.
- If the input field has been focused, it calls `fetchData`

